{-
   What a **view** refuses - `doc/proposal/Analysis-Manifestations.md` Part 8's two properties of a
   representation record, asserted from outside the module that declares it.

   A window is `Array(a)` under a view contract and its bytes are `ArrayView(a)`'s, so field lookup
   is keyed on the occurrence: the owner's fields are not there. And the view record is `@local` to
   Core, so its own fields cannot be read from here either - a program that wants the extent writes
   `length(xs)`, which is the library's body over the field it may not name.
-}

-- The owner's field, on a window. This was accepted and read the owner's field out of the window's
-- two words before lookup was keyed on the occurrence.
fn ownerField(xs: [I32]) -> Size = truncate(xs.run.capacity) :: Size

-- The view's field, from outside Core.
fn viewField(xs: [I32]) -> Size = xs.length

fn main() -> I32 = 0
